IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-fares-minerals.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 393 to 396 (fares, valuable minerals, search for valuable minerals, mines).
-- Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4. A prohibition ("No person ... shall") answers JUST TRUE when every element is met and NOTHING
-- otherwise (a prohibition limited by its own wording: marginal reading (b)); an offence "Every person ... who" answers JUST FALSE when an element is unmet.
-- The s 2 "valuable mineral" is called here with its own inputs: the kind of thing and its value per kilogram.

§ `Part X -- sections 393 to 396`

§§ `Section 393 -- Fraud in relation to fares, etc.`

-- src:7279 | Fraud in relation to fares, etc.
-- src:7280 | 393 (1) Every person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission and who intentionally does any of the following is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction:
-- src:7281 | (a) fails to collect it,
-- src:7282 | (b) collects less than the proper amount payable in respect thereof, or
-- src:7283 | (c) accepts any valuable consideration for failing to collect it or for collecting less than the proper amount payable in respect thereof.
@ref s 393(1) (src:7279-7283)
GIVEN `the person's duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to collect it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person collects less than the proper amount payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person accepts valuable consideration for failing to collect it or for collecting less than the proper amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` MEANS
    IF    `the person's duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission`
      AND `the person acts intentionally`
      AND (   `the person fails to collect it`   -- (a)
           OR `the person collects less than the proper amount payable`   -- (b)
           OR `the person accepts valuable consideration for failing to collect it or for collecting less than the proper amount`)   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission and who intentionally does any of the following"

@ref s 393(1) (the punishments) (src:7279-7283)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 393(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 393(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7279-7283)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 393(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7284 | Idem
-- src:7285 | (2) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who gives or offers to a person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission fee any valuable consideration
-- src:7286 | (a) for failing to collect it, or
-- src:7287 | (b) for collecting an amount less than the amount payable in respect thereof.
@ref s 393(2) (src:7284-7287)
GIVEN `the person gives or offers valuable consideration to a person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration is for failing to collect it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration is for collecting an amount less than the amount payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(2) the conduct is the offence of giving or offering consideration to the person who collects fares` MEANS
    IF `the person gives or offers valuable consideration to a person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission fee` AND (`the consideration is for failing to collect it` OR `the consideration is for collecting an amount less than the amount payable`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who gives or offers to a person whose duty it is to collect a fare, toll, ticket or admission fee any valuable consideration"

@ref s 393(2) (the punishments) (src:7284-7287)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 393(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 393(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7284-7287)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 393(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7288 | Fraudulently obtaining transportation
-- src:7289 | (3) Every one who, by any false pretence or fraud, unlawfully obtains transportation by land, water or air is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 393(3) (src:7288-7289)
GIVEN `the person acts by any false pretence or fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person unlawfully obtains transportation by land, water or air` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 393(3) the conduct is the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation` MEANS
    IF `the person acts by any false pretence or fraud` AND `the person unlawfully obtains transportation by land, water or air`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, by any false pretence or fraud, unlawfully obtains transportation by land, water or air"

@ref s 393(3) (the punishments) (src:7288-7289)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 393(3) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 1: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 393(3) (the class of the offence) (src:7288-7289)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 393(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Section 394 -- Fraud in relation to valuable minerals`

-- The prohibitions ("No person ... shall") are regulative rules with SHANT (ruling N2: where the text names the bearer, the prohibition is derived from the answer). The bearer is "person": the accused.
DECLARE `s 394 act of the accused` IS ONE OF
    `s 394(1) defraud or conceal as the holder of a lease or licence`
    `s 394(2) sell an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral`
    `s 394(3) buy an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral from a person believed not to be the owner`
    `s 394.1(1) possess an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394`

DECLARE `s 394 act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 394(6) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty`
    `s 394.1(4) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty`

-- (1) No person who is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals, shall
-- (a) by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defraud or attempt to defraud any person of (i) any valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence, or (ii) any money or valuable interest or thing payable ...; or
-- (b) fraudulently conceal or make a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence.
-- src:7290 | Fraud in relation to valuable minerals
-- src:7291 | 394 (1) No person who is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals, shall
-- src:7292 | (a) by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defraud or attempt to defraud any person of
-- src:7293 | (i) any valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence, or
-- src:7294 | (ii) any money or valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence; or
-- src:7295 | (b) fraudulently conceal or make a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence.
@ref s 394(1) (src:7290-7295)
GIVEN `the person is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defrauds or attempts to defraud any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is defrauded of valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is defrauded of money or a valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently conceals or makes a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the mineral is` IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person is the holder of a lease or licence issued under an Act relating to the mining of valuable minerals, or by the owner of land that is supposed to contain valuable minerals`
                          , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person, by a fraudulent device or contrivance, defrauds or attempts to defraud any person`   -- (a)
                                                                       , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person is defrauded of valuable minerals obtained under or reserved by the lease or licence`, `s 2 valuable mineral` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`)   -- (a)(i)
                                                                                           , JUST `the person is defrauded of money or a valuable interest or thing payable in respect of valuable minerals obtained or rights reserved by the lease or licence`))   -- (a)(ii)
                                              , `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person fraudulently conceals or makes a false statement with respect to the amount of valuable minerals obtained under the lease or licence`   -- (b)
                                                                       , `s 2 valuable mineral` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`))) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person who is the holder of a lease or licence" shall do (a) or (b); a person outside that description, or an act outside (a) and (b), is outside the prohibition

@ref s 394(1) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7290-7295)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the accused`
`s 394(1) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 394(1) defraud or conceal as the holder of a lease or licence`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) No person, other than the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority, shall sell any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed.
-- src:7296 | Sale of valuable minerals
-- src:7297 | (2) No person, other than the owner or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority, shall sell any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed.
@ref s 394(2) (src:7296-7297)
GIVEN `the person sells the mineral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the mineral is` IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person sells the mineral`, JUST `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed`, JUST (NOT `the person is the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority`), `s 2 valuable mineral` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person, other than the owner or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority, shall sell any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed"

@ref s 394(2) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7296-7297)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the accused`
`s 394(2) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 394(2) sell an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (3) No person shall buy any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed from anyone who the person has reason to believe is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority.
-- src:7298 | Purchase of valuable minerals
-- src:7299 | (3) No person shall buy any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed from anyone who the person has reason to believe is not the owner or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority.
@ref s 394(3) (src:7298-7299)
GIVEN `the person buys the mineral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reason to believe that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the mineral is` IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person buys the mineral`, JUST `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed`, JUST `the person has reason to believe that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority`, `s 2 valuable mineral` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall buy any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed from anyone who the person has reason to believe is not the owner"

@ref s 394(3) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7298-7299)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the accused`
`s 394(3) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 394(3) buy an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral from a person believed not to be the owner`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3), in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, it is presumed that (a) in the case of a sale, the seller is not the owner ...; and (b) in the case of a purchase, the purchaser, when buying ..., had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner ...
-- src:7300 | Presumption
-- src:7301 | (4) In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3), in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, it is presumed that
-- src:7302 | (a) in the case of a sale, the seller is not the owner of the valuable mineral or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority; and
-- src:7303 | (b) in the case of a purchase, the purchaser, when buying the valuable mineral, had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner of the mineral or the owner’s agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority.
@ref s 394(4) (src:7300-7303)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in relation to subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(4)(a) it is presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceeding is in relation to subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3)"
    ELSE IF `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 394(4)(b) (src:7300-7303)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in relation to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(4)(b) it is presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceeding is in relation to subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In any proceeding in relation to subsection (2) or (3)"
    ELSE IF `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (5) A person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3) is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7304 | Offence
-- src:7305 | (5) A person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3) is guilty of
-- src:7306 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7307 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 394(5) (src:7304-7307)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 394(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes subsection (2), by s 394(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes subsection (3), by s 394(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)` MEANS
    `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 394(1)`, `the person contravenes subsection (2), by s 394(2)`, `the person contravenes subsection (3), by s 394(3)`)
    -- JUST TRUE when one is contravened; otherwise NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibitions answer NOTHING outside their limits, and a JUST FALSE input would give JUST FALSE: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3)"

@ref s 394(5) (the punishments) (src:7304-7307)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 394(5) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 394(5) (the class of the offence) (src:7304-7307)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 394(5) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (6) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, to be forfeited to Her Majesty.
-- A power named "may" with an "if" gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1)), fork F7.
-- src:7308 | Forfeiture
-- src:7309 | (6) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed, on such conviction, to be forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref s 394(6) (src:7308-7309)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` AND `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may order anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed"

-- A permission with no LEST: the court MAY order forfeiture.
@ref s 394(6) (the power of the court) (src:7308-7309)
GIVEN `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394(6), subject to subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the court`
`s 394(6) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394(6), subject to subsection (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 394(6) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (7) Subsection (6) does not apply to real property other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under this section.
-- "(other than X)" is decided case by case (the maintainer, 2026-11-05): real property built or modified for the purpose is outside the exception, so (6) reaches it (fork F8).
-- src:7310 | Exception
-- src:7311 | (7) Subsection (6) does not apply to real property other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under this section.
@ref s 394(7) (src:7310-7311)
GIVEN `the thing is real property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the real property was built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the thing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the thing is real property`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception names real property; a thing that is not real property is outside it
    ELSE IF `the real property was built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under this section`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "real property other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under this section"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The power of subsection (6) as cut down by the exception of subsection (7): (7) answering JUST TRUE takes the thing out of (6).
@ref s 394(6) (as cut down by subsection (7)) (src:7310-7311)
GIVEN `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394(6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (6) does not apply to the thing, by s 394(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF `subsection (6) does not apply to the thing, by s 394(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (6) does not apply to real property"
    ELSE `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394(6)`

§§ `Section 394.1 -- Possession of stolen or fraudulently obtained valuable minerals`

-- (1) No person shall possess any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394.
-- src:7312 | Possession of stolen or fraudulently obtained valuable minerals
-- src:7313 | 394.1 (1) No person shall possess any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394.
@ref s 394.1(1) (src:7312-7313)
GIVEN `the person possesses the mineral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the mineral is` IS A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
      `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person possesses the mineral`, JUST `the mineral is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed`, JUST `the mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394`, `s 2 valuable mineral` `what the mineral is` `the value of the mineral, in dollars per kilogram`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall possess any valuable mineral that is unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394"

@ref s 394.1(1) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7312-7313)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the accused`
`s 394.1(1) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 394.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 394.1(1) possess an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) Reasonable grounds to believe that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394 are, in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394.
-- src:7314 | Evidence
-- src:7315 | (2) Reasonable grounds to believe that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394 are, in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary, proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394.
@ref s 394.1(2) (src:7314-7315)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(2) the reasonable grounds are proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` MEANS
    IF NOT `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of reasonable grounds; where there are none it is silent
    ELSE IF `there is evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence raising a reasonable doubt to the contrary"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7316 | Offence
-- src:7317 | (3) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7318 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7319 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 394.1(3) (src:7316-7319)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 394.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(3) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the person contravenes subsection (1), by s 394.1(1)`   -- JUST TRUE when it is contravened; NOTHING carried from the prohibition's own limit

@ref s 394.1(3) (the punishments) (src:7316-7319)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 394.1(3) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 394.1(3) (the class of the offence) (src:7316-7319)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 394.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may, on that conviction, order that anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed be forfeited to Her Majesty.
-- src:7320 | Forfeiture
-- src:7321 | (4) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may, on that conviction, order that anything by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed be forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref s 394.1(4) (src:7320-7321)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under this section` AND `the thing is something by means of or in relation to which the offence was committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court may, on that conviction, order"

@ref s 394.1(4) (the power of the court) (src:7320-7321)
GIVEN `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394.1(4), subject to subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 394 act of the court`
`s 394.1(4) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394.1(4), subject to subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 394.1(4) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (5) Subsection (4) does not apply to real property, other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under subsection (3).
-- src:7322 | Exception
-- src:7323 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply to real property, other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under subsection (3).
@ref s 394.1(5) (src:7322-7323)
GIVEN `the thing is real property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the real property was built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the thing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the thing is real property`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception names real property; a thing that is not real property is outside it
    ELSE IF `the real property was built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under subsection (3)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than real property built or significantly modified for the purpose of facilitating the commission of an offence under subsection (3)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 394.1(4) (as cut down by subsection (5)) (src:7322-7323)
GIVEN `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) does not apply to the thing, by s 394.1(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `subsection (4) does not apply to the thing, by s 394.1(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply to real property"
    ELSE `the court may order forfeiture, by s 394.1(4)`

§§ `Section 395 -- Search for valuable minerals`

-- (1) If an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice by a peace officer or by a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the
-- enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to this Act or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person,
-- the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer, if the public officer is named in it, to search any of the places or persons mentioned in the information.
-- For the person searched this is what may be done to them. The justice's power is stated with an "if": NOTHING when the gate fails (fork F7). The informant's status is the keel's answer, taken as an input.
-- src:7324 | Search for valuable minerals
-- src:7325 | 395 (1) If an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice by a peace officer or by a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament and the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to this Act or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person, the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer, if the public officer is named in it, to search any of the places or persons mentioned in the information.
@ref s 395(1) (src:7324-7325)
GIVEN `an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the informant is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the informant is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the public officer has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and its duties include the enforcement of the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice`
                          , `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the informant is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer`
                                               , `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the informant is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`, JUST `the public officer has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and its duties include the enforcement of the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament`))
                          , JUST `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that, contrary to the Criminal Code or any other Act of Parliament, any valuable mineral is deposited in a place or held by a person`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an information in writing is laid under oath before a justice by a peace officer or by a public officer ... and the justice is satisfied ... the justice may issue a warrant"

@ref s 395(1) (who the warrant authorizes) (src:7324-7325)
GIVEN `the officer is a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public officer is named in the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1) the warrant authorizes the officer to search` MEANS
    IF `the officer is a peace officer` OR (`the officer is a public officer` AND `the public officer is named in the warrant`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "authorizing a peace officer or a public officer, if the public officer is named in it"

-- (1.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
-- src:7326 | Execution in Canada
-- src:7327 | (1.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer, who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref s 395(1.1) (src:7326-7327)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1.1) the warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be executed at any place in Canada"

@ref s 395(1.1) (the officer who executes it) (src:7326-7327)
GIVEN `the officer is a public officer named in the warrant or a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(1.1) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the officer is a public officer named in the warrant or a peace officer`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is stated for "A public officer named in the warrant, or any peace officer"
    ELSE IF `the officer has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed"

-- (2) If, on search, anything mentioned in subsection (1) is found, it shall be seized and brought before a justice of the province in which the warrant was issued who has jurisdiction in the matter, and the justice shall order
-- (a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial; or (b) if it is not detained ..., (i) that it be restored to the owner, or (ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province ... if the owner cannot be ascertained.
-- src:7328 | Power to seize
-- src:7329 | (2) If, on search, anything mentioned in subsection (1) is found, it shall be seized and brought before a justice of the province in which the warrant was issued who has jurisdiction in the matter, and the justice shall order
-- src:7330 | (a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial; or
-- src:7331 | (b) if it is not detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial,
-- src:7332 | (i) that it be restored to the owner, or
-- src:7333 | (ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place if the owner cannot be ascertained.
@ref s 395(2) (src:7328-7333)
GIVEN `on search, anything mentioned in subsection (1) is found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(2) the thing found shall be seized and brought before a justice` MEANS
    IF `on search, anything mentioned in subsection (1) is found`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on search, anything mentioned in subsection (1) is found, it shall be seized"

DECLARE `s 395(2) order of the justice` IS ONE OF
    `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
    `s 395(2)(b)(i) that it be restored to the owner`
    `s 395(2)(b)(ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place`

-- Fork F9: (b)(i) carries no condition and (b)(ii) is "if the owner cannot be ascertained". Taken: (i) when the owner can be ascertained, (ii) when not.
@ref s 395(2) (the order the justice shall make) (src:7329-7333)
GIVEN `the thing is detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner can be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 395(2) order of the justice`
`s 395(2) the order the justice shall make` MEANS
    IF `the thing is detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
    THEN `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
    ELSE IF `the owner can be ascertained`
         THEN `s 395(2)(b)(i) that it be restored to the owner`
         ELSE `s 395(2)(b)(ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place`

DECLARE `s 395(2) act of the justice` IS ONE OF
    `s 395(2) order that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
    `s 395(2) order that it be restored to the owner`
    `s 395(2) order that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place`

-- The duty of the justice: MUST make the order the function above settles. No time limit and no consequence are stated.
@ref s 395(2) (the duty of the justice) (src:7328-7333)
GIVEN order IS A `s 395(2) order of the justice`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 395(2) act of the justice`
`s 395(2) the duty of the justice` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial` THEN PARTY `a justice` MUST `s 395(2) order that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
    WHEN `s 395(2)(b)(i) that it be restored to the owner` THEN PARTY `a justice` MUST `s 395(2) order that it be restored to the owner`
    WHEN `s 395(2)(b)(ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place` THEN PARTY `a justice` MUST `s 395(2) order that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place`

-- (3) An appeal lies from an order made under paragraph (2)(b) in the manner in which an appeal lies in summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII and the provisions of that Part relating to appeals apply to appeals under this subsection.
-- The manner of appeal is Part XXVII's (another part: points outside this range); only the existence of the appeal is answered here.
-- src:7334 | Appeal
-- src:7335 | (3) An appeal lies from an order made under paragraph (2)(b) in the manner in which an appeal lies in summary conviction proceedings under Part XXVII and the provisions of that Part relating to appeals apply to appeals under this subsection.
@ref s 395(3) (src:7334-7335)
GIVEN `the order was made under paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 395(3) an appeal lies from the order` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under paragraph (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal lies from an order made under paragraph (2)(b)"; an order under paragraph (2)(a) is not mentioned

§§ `Section 396 -- Offences in relation to mines`

-- (1) Every person ... who (a) adds anything to or removes anything from any existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation ...; or
-- (b) adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material ... taken ... from any existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued, with a fraudulent intent to affect the result ...
-- src:7336 | Offences in relation to mines
-- src:7337 | 396 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:7338 | (a) adds anything to or removes anything from any existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation that has been made or is to be made with respect to the mine, mining claim or oil well, or
-- src:7339 | (b) adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material that has been taken or is being or is about to be taken from any existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued, with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation.
@ref s 396(1) (src:7336-7339)
GIVEN `the person adds anything to or removes anything from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material taken from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` MEANS
    IF (   `the person adds anything to or removes anything from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well`   -- (a)
        OR `the person adds anything to, removes anything from or tampers with a sample or material taken from an existing or prospective mine, mining claim or oil well for the purpose of being assayed, tested or otherwise valued`)   -- (b)
       AND `the person acts with a fraudulent intent to affect the result of the assay, test or valuation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who"

@ref s 396(1) (the punishments) (src:7336-7339)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 396(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 396(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7336-7339)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 396(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) For the purposes of proceedings under subsection (1), evidence that (a) something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or (b) anything to which subsection (1) applies has been tampered with,
-- is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation.
-- src:7340 | Presumption
-- src:7341 | (2) For the purposes of proceedings under subsection (1), evidence that
-- src:7342 | (a) something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or
-- src:7343 | (b) anything to which subsection (1) applies has been tampered with,
-- src:7344 | is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation.
@ref s 396(2) (src:7340-7344)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or that it has been tampered with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of proceedings under subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that something has been added to or removed from anything to which subsection (1) applies, or that it has been tampered with`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes that evidence proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
